<title>INDIA: Indian soyoil prices fall, soybean markets closed.</title>
<headline>Indian soyoil prices fall, soybean markets closed.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean markets were closed on Thursday for a local festival while soyoil prices, for which trading was held, fell, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soybean markets are also closed on Friday for another festival and reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers said soyoil solvent fell by 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined by 100 rupees. Undertone was weak due to limited demand.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices eased slightly on limited export demand. Soymeal yellow was $297 per tonne for current season and $284-285 per for November, December and January shipments. Rapeseed extraction was $132 in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,450 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,400 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
